## 3.11 Verification Reference

### Purpose

The Verification Reference section identifies the approved verification approach and associated engineering artifacts used to demonstrate that a System Objective has been satisfied.

Its purpose is to establish a consistent link between the objective and its verification evidence without embedding detailed verification procedures.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective shall include the following fields:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Verification Method | Approved method used to verify the objective (e.g., Inspection, Analysis, Demonstration, Test). |
| Verification Reference | Reference to the governing verification document or plan. |
| Verification Criteria | High-level criteria defining successful verification. |
| Verification Status | Current verification state of the objective. |
| Verification Evidence | Reference to the evidence produced during verification, where applicable. |

---

### Verification Rules

Verification information shall:

- Reference approved verification artifacts.
- Use only approved verification methods.
- Remain consistent with the Objective Governance framework.
- Be updated as verification activities progress.
- Preserve links to all verification evidence.

---

### Engineering Note

Verification demonstrates that the system has met the objective as specified.

Detailed verification procedures, test cases, and execution records belong in dedicated verification documents rather than within the objective itself.
